      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting an \"Access Denied\" error when my lambda function tries to write logs to this s3 bucket. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u look at this policy and tell me what i missed?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The error likely occurs because the IAM role attached to your Lambda function doesn't have an explicit `s3:*` wildcard action, or the bucket policy doesn't explicitly allow the Lambda execution role to place objects with prefixes like `/logs/`. Most critically, Lambda assumes a specific IAM role at launch time; ensure that role is truly trusted and that it has explicit `s3:PutObject` permissions on the specific bucket resource ARN without relying on stack-overrides. Double-check that the Lambda function's execution role is the one defined as the principal in the S3 bucket policy.",
